      "id": "ai-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Enemies that are toys too",
      "number": "01",
      "eyebrow": "AI behaviour"
    },
    {
      "id": "ai-intro",
      "type": "text",
      "html": "<p>The goal was distinct AI behaviours for a satirical, toy-themed souls-like sandbox: maximum readability and mechanical variation across encounters, leaning on unconventional silhouettes and physics-driven locomotion.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "rules-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "The rule set I designed against"
    },
    {
      "id": "rules",
      "type": "pillars",
      "items": [
        {
          "label": "Asset differentiation",
          "body": "High visual and mechanical contrast, with its own silhouette boundary and movement profile for each of the 15 archetypes."
        },
        {
          "label": "Dynamic threat caps",
          "body": "Strict population ceilings for swarm-type enemies, to keep visual clutter and player cognitive load under control."
        },
        {
          "label": "Dynamic hit-stop scaling",
          "body": "Algorithmic frame pauses mapped to asset mass and velocity, so impact feedback reads at a glance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-h",
      "type": "text",
